{"name":"Bagel","hex":"#f6cd9b","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bagel","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A toroidal bread roll that is boiled before it is baked.","A score of 6-0 in a set (after the shape of a bagel, which looks like a zero)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To achieve a score of 6–0 (as the winner) in a tennis set.","To hold an opponent to a score of zero."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bagel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bagel","blocks":[{"text":"A bagel is a bread roll originating in the Jewish communities of Poland. Bagels are traditionally made from yeasted wheat dough that is shaped by hand into a torus or ring, briefly boiled in water, and then baked. The result is a dense, chewy, doughy interior with a browned and sometimes crisp exterior."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Bagel_with_sesame_3.jpg/330px-Bagel_with_sesame_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bagel","wikidata":"Q272502"},{"title":"Bagel (tennis)","blocks":[{"text":"In tennis, a bagel is when the set ends with a score of 6–0. An extremely rare type of bagel, where no point is lost, is called a golden set. Most bagel sets occur in the early rounds of tennis tournaments where the favorites play lower-ranked players, such as lucky losers or wild cards."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bagel_(tennis)","wikidata":"Q30337019"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/%2Athis%2A_is_a_bagel.jpg/500px-%2Athis%2A_is_a_bagel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/%2Athis%2A_is_a_bagel.jpg/1280px-%2Athis%2A_is_a_bagel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/%2Athis%2A_is_a_bagel.jpg/500px-%2At